    "body": "## What\n\n- Citar shows an emoji for the entry type (first column) instead of the type name.\n- `sp-org-tag-groups` gets the 14 BibTeX types as `sp-org-tag-groups-bibtex-types` (type, emoji, litnote tag), generating one rule per Org tag.\n- Registry: literature group gains `proceedings`, `inproceedings`, `manual`, `report`, `manuscript`.\n- Docs: new \"Literature note tags\" section with the mapping as a table, where the tags deviate from BibTeX, and how to unify them.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `text` is shared by booklet and misc, so the tag shows 📔️ (first type wins).\n- Unknown types fall back to 📄️.\n- Not yet tried in the GUI; run `citar-refresh` after loading.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
